; wf_port_7c0001: Writes 0xAC and then 0xFF to the low byte of control_and_link (0x7c0001), each
;   followed by 27 calls to the link poll 0xa4962, which reads bit 5 of 0x7c0000. It is 54 bytes and
;   runs once per frame right before the blit burst. Guarded by 0x20bc98: if that is not zero, it
;   does nothing. The reading of the two values as half scanline widths is refuted under
;   control_and_link in registers.yaml
