; wf_raster_band: Handler of the band ABOVE the horizon: pins the scroll at 257, which is the
;   scenery's first row in the plane, that is a stop against its top edge
wf_raster_band:
000dc7c6  33ee040000740000      move.w (0x400,A6),(soundlatch).l  ; soundlatch
000dc7ce  548e                  addq.l 0x2,A6

; wf_road_scroll: Writes word 8 as the constant 0x80 (y bit 8 set, page bit ZERO) on each line of
;   the band above the road, then y=1 at 0xdc7d8. MEASURED with a per-site write log over an attract
;   cycle: 10489 writes at vpos 1..53, the page bit zero in all of them. It is the one that made the
;   page look as if it varied per line, and why the boundary moved with the HORIZON: on those lines
;   the page really is zero
