; wf_clip_dispatch: Entry of the software clipper: scales the descriptor's width and height through
;   wf_scale_coord, rejects a zero size, and branches to one of eight variants by the complement of
;   D2's low three bits (bit 0 set: x walks forward; bit 1 set: y walks forward; bit 2 clear: the
;   axes are exchanged). Every variant rejects what lies wholly outside the rectangle
;   wf_clip_x0..wf_clip_y1 and pins to its edge an end that crosses it; when the pinned end is the
;   walk's start, it flips that axis's direction bit and takes the source from its other end, so the
;   walk ends on the edge
wf_clip_dispatch:
000e484e  48e77fc0              movem.l {  A1 A0 D7 D6 D5 D4 D3 D2 D1},-(SP)
